    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-ceiling matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers our highest daily efficiency score of 83.29. Facing Canning, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable SP xERA of 4.36, making him the clear anchor of the lineup. In the outfield, **Kyle Tucker** (75.69) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) follow closely behind. **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly intriguing start; beyond his strong park adjustment, his score is bolstered by a 90% probability of a stolen base opportunity against a slow-working pitcher, aligning perfectly with our strategy to prioritize speed in this 5x5 Roto environment. **Andy Pages** also draws a strong 71.61 score, leveraging a high SP skill adjustment against Kay to provide stability in the outfield.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involved **Josh Jung**, who landed at 55.18. While **Josh Jung** is a viable producer, he narrowly missed the cut behind **Coby Mayo** and **Miguel Vargas**, who both benefitted from more favorable platoon or park environments relative to their spots in the order. We are also monitoring **Liam Hicks** closely; his score of 44.69 is our lowest in the starting nine, pushed down by the challenge of facing Ashcraft, but his lead-off spot keeps his efficiency above our floor requirement. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on **Sam Antonacci** at the top of the order to provide the necessary speed and on-base presence against Sasaki. No immediate weather alerts threaten the slate, but we remain cautious regarding the lower-scoring plays like **Dominic Smith**; his 40.24 score is approaching our benching threshold, and we will be ready to swap him if mid-day lineup adjustments indicate a decline in his opportunity.",
